-- C29 example: long horizontal producer with tubing friction and inflow-control devices (FlexWell-lite).
-- Base reservoir = DEPLETION.DATA (15x15x3, solution-gas drive). PROD is a 5200 ft horizontal well in layer 2 along I
-- (heel at I=2, toe at I=14) on BHP control. The RESSIM WELLBORE line gives a 4 in (0.333 ft) tubing, roughness 5e-5 ft and
-- an ICD (K 2e-5 psi/(rb/d)^2) at every connection: dp_ICD = K (rho_mix / rho_cal) q^2. The friction pressure is accumulated from the heel
-- (first connection) to the toe, so toe connections see a higher well pressure and contribute less; the ICDs even the
-- inflow along the well. Results: Custom plots well vector WDPWB (wellbore + ICD drop at the deepest connection), WOPR,
-- WGOR. Compare with the same deck without the RESSIM line (or set "On" off in Advanced ->
-- Wellbore friction and ICD). OPM Flow ignores the RESSIM line (plain well).
-- Expected (BHP 2500 psi, first 91 days): FOPR 17453 (no wellbore) -> 16315 (friction only, 224 psi at the toe)
-- -> 10726 stb/d (friction + ICD, 394 psi); after 5 years FOPT 5.948e6 -> 5.960e6 -> 5.961e6 stb with less gas
-- (5.425e9 -> 5.413e9 scf): the ICD slows the early, gas-rich heel inflow. Runs in ~2 s.
-- Lines starting with '-- RESSIM:' carry settings ECLIPSE has no keyword for (ignored by ECLIPSE).

